cff-version: 1.2.0
title: NanoKMC
message: >-
  If you use the NanoKMC Active-Filtered method in scientific work, please
  cite the accompanying NanoKMC paper once its final bibliographic record is
  available, and cite this software release when appropriate.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Prüfer
    given-names: Thomas
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-21
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  Single-core C++17 research implementation of the NanoKMC Active-Filtered
  lattice kinetic Monte Carlo formulation and controlled classical,
  partial-filter, rate-category, and exact-class reference solvers for the
  binary FCC Kawasaki-exchange benchmark.
keywords:
  - kinetic Monte Carlo
  - lattice kinetic Monte Carlo
  - Kawasaki dynamics
  - binary alloy
  - active-event filtering
  - Monte Carlo
  - research software
  - reproducibility
